  "query_preview": "..\n\nKey Message 1)\n\nNorthwest flow aloft continues with a weak front dropping southeast \nthrough the area tonight. Southwesterly flow ahead of the front will\nusher in a warmer air today, allowing high temperatures- to climb \ninto the upper 70s to lower 80s. \n\nThe weak cold front moves through tonight, but do not expect any \npcpn with this passage. The main impact will be temperatures dipping \ncloser to normal values on Thursday and Friday before quickly \nrebounding again on Saturday. A mid level ridge will build into the\narea for Saturday which looks to be the warmest day of the week, \nwith most locations reaching the lower 80s. \n\nThe main feature to monitor for the second half of the weekend will\nbe the track of tropical remnants from the Gulf. A number of\ndeterministic model solutions and ensembles indicate that this low \nwill track north into ILN/s FA, which would bring widespread \nprecipitation to the area Sunday. Will continue to monitor forecast\ntrends before diving into the details.",
